 1. Chosen Development Model
Development Model
Agile Model

Justification
The Agile model was selected because it allows the team to develop the system step by step and make improvements throughout the project. Since the School Event Management System includes different roles such as admin, student, and student club president, Agile is suitable because it gives flexibility when adding or adjusting features. It also helps the team divide work efficiently, test parts of the system regularly, and solve issues early.

---

2. User Requirements

a. Stakeholders

1. Students
Students are the main users of the system. They want an easy way to view school events, check timetables based on their department or clubs, and apply for mentorship opportunities.

2. Admin
The admin manages the overall system. Their interest is to control users, departments, clubs, events, and ensure the platform works properly.

3. Student Club Presidents
Student club presidents are responsible for organizing and managing club-related events. They need the ability to create, update, and manage events for their club members.

4. Student Mentors
Student mentors offer mentorship support to other students. They need to be visible in the system so that students can apply for guidance or mentorship.

5. Development Team
The development team designs, codes, tests, and maintains the system. Their goal is to build a working, secure, and user-friendly application.

---

b. User Stories

User Story 1
As a student, I want to view event timetables based on my department so that I can easily find academic events that are relevant to me.

User Story 2
As a student, I want to view events related to my clubs so that I do not miss club meetings, activities, or conferences.

User Story 3
As a student, I want to apply for mentorship from a student mentor so that I can receive academic or personal guidance.

User Story 4
As an admin, I want to manage all users and events so that the system stays organized and updated.

User Story 5
As a student club president, I want to create and manage club events so that club members can see accurate and updated event information.

User Story 6
As an admin, I want to assign departments and clubs properly so that event visibility is correctly organized.

User Story 7
As a student mentor, I want to receive mentorship requests so that I can support students who need guidance.

User Story 8
As a user, I want to log in securely based on my role so that I can access the correct features of the system.

---

3. Functional Requirements

a. Description

1. User Registration and Login
The system should allow users to register and log in according to their role.

2. Role-Based Access
The system should provide different access levels for students, admins, and student club presidents.

3. Event Viewing
The system should allow students to view events by department and by club.

4. Timetable Display
The system should display event schedules in an organized timetable format.

5. Event Management
The system should allow admins and club presidents to create, edit, and delete events.

6. Mentorship Application
The system should allow students to apply for mentorship opportunities from available student mentors.

7. User Management
The admin should be able to manage user accounts and roles.

8. Club and Department Management
The admin should be able to manage departments and student clubs in the system.

---

b. Acceptance Criteria

Feature: User Registration and Login
Acceptance Criteria:
- User enters valid registration details
- System creates the account successfully
- User enters valid username or email and password
- System verifies credentials
- User is redirected to the correct dashboard based on role
- Error message is shown for invalid login details

Feature: Role-Based Access
Acceptance Criteria:
- Students can only access student features
- Club presidents can access club event management features
- Admin can access all management features
- Unauthorized users cannot access restricted pages

Feature: Event Viewing
Acceptance Criteria:
- Student can see events related to their department
- Student can see events related to their club
- Event details include title, date, time, location, and organizer
- Events are displayed clearly and correctly

Feature: Timetable Display
Acceptance Criteria:
- Events are shown in date and time order
- Students can view timetable without errors
- Timetable updates when new events are added
- Timetable only shows relevant events based on user category

Feature: Event Management
Acceptance Criteria:
- Admin and club president can create events
- Admin and club president can edit event details
- Admin and club president can delete events
- Changes are saved correctly in the database

Feature: Mentorship Application
Acceptance Criteria:
- Student can view available mentors
- Student can submit a mentorship request
- System stores mentorship request successfully
- Mentor or admin can review the request

Feature: User Management
Acceptance Criteria:
- Admin can add users
- Admin can edit user roles
- Admin can deactivate or remove users
- User data is updated correctly in the system

Feature: Club and Department Management
Acceptance Criteria:
- Admin can add clubs and departments
- Admin can update club and department information
- Events can be linked to correct clubs and departments
- Invalid or duplicate entries are prevented where necessary

