5. Application Specifications

a. Architecture
The system follows a three-tier architecture:
- Frontend: provides the user interface for students, admins, club presidents, and mentors
- Backend: handles business logic such as login, role management, event creation, and mentorship requests
- Database: stores users, events, clubs, departments, and mentorship applications

The frontend sends requests to the backend. The backend processes these requests, applies the business rules, and communicates with the database to save or retrieve data.

---

b. Database Model
The database will include tables such as:

- Users
- Roles
- Departments
- Clubs
- Events
- MentorshipRequests
- Mentors

Relationships
- Each user has one role
- A student may belong to one department and possibly one or more clubs
- Each event may be linked to a department or a club
- Mentorship requests are linked to a student and a mentor

Constraints
- User email must be unique
- Each event must have a valid organizer
- Department and club IDs must reference existing records
- Mentorship requests must reference valid student and mentor accounts

